@title Late Sales Dashboards Postmortem
@subtitle Juniper Retail, 2026-10-02
@author Analytics Platform

## Impact

- 9 hours of delay: dashboards normally ready by 02:00 were refreshed at 10:58.
- 23 dashboards stale.
- The 08:00 executive sales report went out with the previous day's numbers.

## Pipeline

diagram flow dir=LR title="Nightly sales pipeline"
flow: ordersdb "Orders DB" db
flow: cdc "CDC Connector" svc
flow: kafka "Kafka" queue
flow: spark "Spark Job" fn "failed: OOM" focus
flow: wh "Warehouse" db
flow: dash "Dashboards" user
flow: ordersdb -> cdc -> kafka
flow: kafka -> spark : orders topic
flow: spark -> wh -> dash

## Timeline

table = Time,Event; 01:00,Nightly Spark Job starts; 01:47,Spark Job fails with out-of-memory on the orders partition for 2026-10-01; 02:30,Automatic retry also fails; 07:55,Analyst reports stale dashboards; 08:20,On-call doubles executor memory to 16 GB and reruns; 10:05,Spark Job succeeds; 10:58,Dashboards refreshed

## Root cause

A promotion on 2026-10-01 produced 3.4 times the normal order volume: 4.1 million orders against a typical 1.2 million. The Spark Job's executors had a fixed 8 GB of memory each, which was not enough to process the oversized orders partition, so both the scheduled run and the automatic retry failed with out-of-memory errors. Because a failed retry did not page anyone, the failure went unnoticed until an analyst reported stale dashboards.

## Lessons learned

### What went well

- Once on-call was engaged, the cause was found and fixed within 25 minutes.
- Doubling executor memory let the rerun complete without code changes.

### What did not go well

- Two consecutive failures did not page anyone.
- Executor memory was fixed and ignored input volume.
- Dashboards gave no sign that their data was stale.

## Action items

1. Page on-call when the nightly job fails twice.
2. Size executor memory from the input volume.
3. Add a data freshness banner to dashboards.
